      "aiExplanation": {
        "simpleDefinition": "A ledger is an account that tracks all money movement for a person, company, bank, or expense head.",
        "businessContext": "If a customer buys goods, their ledger shows how much they owe, what they paid, and what remains due. If you open a bank account, that bank's ledger shows every deposit and withdrawal.",
